    {
      "question": "Is the lunar rover safer with the fans off?",
      "question_key": "is the lunar rover safer with the fans off",
      "habitat": "lunar_rover",
      "fingerprint": "8c1c5d4fd81bf87e9712775a57d07d1b4d185fb467019443a3336824e2605050",
      "intent": "fans_off",
      "mode_generated": "template",
      "answer_markdown": "Lunar rover: 1.62 m/s² (0.165 g), 8.2 psia, 34% O₂, vent 5 cm/s, flame size 10 mm.\n\n**With the fans on:** **Regime: buoyant.** For Lunar rover the buoyant velocity is 25.5 cm/s against a vent flow of 5 cm/s, so the Richardson number Ri = u_b²/u_f² is 25.9 (forced Ri < 0.1, buoyant Ri > 10) [eng:physics]. Sampling the uncertain constants gives 0% forced, 11.9% mixed and 88.1% buoyant flames [eng:physics].\n\n**With the fans off:** **Regime: buoyant.** For Lunar rover with fans off the buoyant velocity is 25.5 cm/s against a vent flow of 0 cm/s, so the Richardson number Ri = u_b²/u_f² is unbounded (no forced flow) (forced Ri < 0.1, buoyant Ri > 10) [eng:fans_off:physics]. Sampling the uncertain constants gives 0% forced, 0% mixed and 100% buoyant flames [eng:fans_off:physics].\n\nFans on: **M1 – P(droplet flame self-extinguishes before burnout)**: estimate 20.1%, 90% band 0.727% to 76.2% [eng:M1]. The microgravity-only band is 3.9% to 48.2%. Transfer confidence: **low**.\n\nFans off: **M1 – P(droplet flame self-extinguishes before burnout)**: estimate 20.1%, 90% band 0.653% to 77.6% [eng:fans_off:M1]. The microgravity-only band is 3.9% to 48.2%. Transfer confidence: **low**.\n\n**Not safer by this evidence.** Without ventilation the flame is not microgravity-like: buoyancy takes over and the 90% band gets wider. For M1–M3 the engine never shifts the estimate with gravity or flow (gravity honesty rule), it only widens the band, so 'safer' cannot be claimed from these data.\n\nDesign implication: At lunar gravity a 10 mm flame becomes buoyancy-dominated (Ri > 10) when the vent flow is below about 8.0 cm/s (median coefficients): turning ventilation off does not create a microgravity-like quiescent flame. [eng:design:2]",
